{"id":4191,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/superlative-adjectives/","parentId":540,"order":200,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Superlative adjectives: The oldest, the most important, etc.","seo":{"title":"Superlative adjectives: The oldest, the most important, etc. - Test-English","description":"Master superlative adjectives in English with our A1 elementary English lesson. A grammar chart, fun exercises and lots of examples await!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_Superlative-adjectives.png"},"modified":"2026-02-19T08:27:44","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Write the superlative forms of these adjectives.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: poor ⇒ <span class=\"textGap\">the poorest</span></em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"483\"></div> <p></p>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct superlative or comparative forms to complete these sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"484\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Write superlative adjectives using the adjectives in brackets. Include <em>the</em>.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: She is <span class=\"textGap\">the most intelligent</span> (intelligent) student in my class.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"485\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>Superlative adjectives</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-19714\" src=\"/media/uploads/Comparative-superlative-adjectives_A2-new.png\" alt=\"Color-coded grammar chart outlining the rules for forming comparative and superlative adjectives based on syllable count and irregular forms.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Three or more things</h4> <p>We use the superlative form of an <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/adverbs-manner/\">adjective or adverb</a> to compare <strong>three or more things</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Both John and his brother play football, but John is <span><strong>better</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>John and his two brothers all play football, but John is<span><strong> the best</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>The best in</strong></h4> <p>After the superlative we use <strong>in</strong>&nbsp;before names of places or before singular words referring to groups of people (<strong>class, school, team, family, etc</strong>.)</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>The Everest is the highest mountain <span><strong>of the world</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>The Everest is the highest mountain <span><strong>in the world</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>She is the best student <span><strong>in the class</strong></span>. </em></li> <li><em>He’s the tallest <span><strong>in the family</strong></span>.</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>The / my / John’s</strong></h4> <p>Before the superlative we always use <strong>the</strong> or a possessive adjective (<strong>my, your, his, etc</strong>.) or noun + <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/whose-possessive-s/\">possessive <strong>‘s</strong></a> (<strong>Paul’s, Elisabeth’s, etc</strong>.)</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>He is <span><strong>the</strong></span> best. </em></li> <li><em>This is <span><strong>my</strong></span> most expensive jacket.</em></li> <li><em>This is <span><strong>Paul’s</strong></span> best friend.</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":483,"questions":[{"id":4224,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>young ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4225,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>sad ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4226,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>remote ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4227,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>smelly ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4228,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>bad ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4229,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>amazing ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4230,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>pretty ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4231,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>flat ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4232,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>short ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4233,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>exciting ⇒ <span data-gap=\"0\"></span></p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]},{"id":484,"questions":[{"id":4234,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Which is _____ planet from the sun?</div>","choices":[{"id":6102,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the farest</span>"},{"id":6103,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the most far</span>"},{"id":6104,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the farthest</span>"}]},{"id":4236,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>_____ the world lives in Indonesia.</div>","choices":[{"id":6105,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>The oldest man of</span>"},{"id":6106,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>The oldest man in</span>"},{"id":6107,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>The most old man of</span>"}]},{"id":4237,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>David is very good at playing football, but Jason is _____.</div>","choices":[{"id":6108,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>best </span>"},{"id":6109,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the best</span>"},{"id":6110,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>better</span>"}]},{"id":4238,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>It was _____ day of my life.</div>","choices":[{"id":6111,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the most happy</span>"},{"id":6112,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the most happiest</span>"},{"id":6113,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the happiest</span>"}]},{"id":4239,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>What is _____ phone on the market?</div>","choices":[{"id":6114,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the thinnest</span>"},{"id":6115,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>thinnest </span>"},{"id":6116,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the most thin</span>"}]},{"id":4240,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Last summer was _____ season ever recorded. </div>","choices":[{"id":6117,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the dryest</span>"},{"id":6118,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the most dry</span>"},{"id":6119,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the driest </span>"}]},{"id":4241,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I'm 10 years _____ than my wife.</div>","choices":[{"id":6120,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>oldest</span>"},{"id":6121,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the oldest</span>"},{"id":6122,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>older</span>"}]},{"id":4242,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He is _____ person in my life.</div>","choices":[{"id":6123,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the most important</span>"},{"id":6124,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the more important</span>"},{"id":6125,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the importantest</span>"}]},{"id":4243,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Our graduates earn _____ salaries in every U.S. state. </div>","choices":[{"id":6126,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the higher</span>"},{"id":6127,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the highest</span>"},{"id":6128,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the most high</span>"}]},{"id":4244,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>That was _____ moment of my life. </div>","choices":[{"id":6129,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>the sadest</span>"},{"id":6130,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>the saddest</span>"},{"id":6131,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>the most sad</span>"}]}]},{"id":485,"questions":[{"id":4223,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>July is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (dry) month in southern Spain. It hardly ever rains. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4235,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p> One World Trade Center is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (tall) building in New York.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4245,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (healthy) person I know. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4246,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Egypt is one of <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (ancient) civilizations.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4247,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He was <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (fast) runner in 2017.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4248,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What month is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (hot) in Scotland?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4249,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She described her year in Singapore as <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (amazing) experience of her life.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4250,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>What is <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (bad) neighbourhood in London?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4251,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>It was <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (slow) car on the circuit.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4252,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We sell <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> (red) and most perfect apples.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}